Goal
All UI colors (bubbles, header, composer, badges, avatars, buttons, tab bar) come from ONE theme engine (`KroTheme` / `ThemeStore`). No hard-coded neon colors inside screens. Neon keeps its levels (Off / Balanced / Full) and is lowered automatically with Reduce Motion and Low Power Mode. Keep Telegram's layout and behavior; only the visual layer changes.

1) Background types
- Solid; gradient (2-5 colors, angle, linear/radial/angular); animated aurora (blob count, speed, size, blur); mesh gradient with draggable points; patterns (dots, lines, grid, geometric; density + opacity); photo from the user's library (crop/move, blur 0-100%, dim, saturation, optional light parallax).
- At least 10 ready-made backgrounds drawn in code (SwiftUI/Canvas). No images or assets taken from Telegram.
- Scope: global, per chat type (private/groups/channels), per single chat. The most specific wins.
- Telegram's own chat background (`setChatBackground`) is optional, separate, and changed only after explicit confirmation. Local backgrounds are never sent anywhere.

2) Automatic neon from the background
- On background change, extract the dominant color ON-DEVICE only (downscale, then cluster) and derive a harmonious neon color (shift in HSL/OKLCH, do not just copy the color).
- Modes: Auto (follows background), Manual (user fixed color), Hybrid (auto plus offsets for hue/saturation/brightness).
- Readability guarantee: text contrast against the bubble background >= 4.5:1. If it fails, adjust the color or add a light scrim automatically. Neon must never make text unreadable.
- Pick neon separately for light and dark appearance when needed.

3) Neon Studio screen (inside Settings > Appearance)
- Per element, switchable and individually colorable: outgoing bubbles, incoming bubbles, header, composer, send button, unread badges, avatars, cards, primary buttons, tab bar.
- Per element: color or two-color gradient, intensity, glow radius, layers (1-4), spread, opacity, glowing border (width/color), pulse (speed/amplitude), breathing, slow hue rotation, touch reaction.
- Presets: Cyber, Pastel, Fire, Ice, Pure OLED Black, Calm (no glow). Presets can be duplicated, edited and saved.
- Live preview on the same screen (sample bubbles, header, composer) and a Reset button per section.
- Safety caps: max intensity, layers and glow area; at most one heavy animated effect per screen; all motion off with Reduce Motion.

4) Storage and sharing
- All settings are Codable fields in `KroTheme` with a schema version and a migration from the current version. Existing user themes must survive.
- JSON export/import keeps the current validation (size limit, count limit, color-format check, clamped ranges, fresh IDs on import).
- Background photos stay local (Application Support, file protection), downscaled (max about 2048 px), excluded from export by default, never uploaded. Exporting with the image is optional and confirmed.

5) Performance
- TimelineView at 24 fps or less for motion; cache rendered backgrounds; `drawingGroup` where it helps. No full redraw per frame.
- Test with a long chat list and a long chat; if effects must be reduced, do it automatically and tell the user.
- VoiceOver and Dynamic Type must work on every background.

6) Required tests
- Dominant-color extraction and neon derivation (simple test images with expected values).
- Contrast guarantee (pass and fail cases).
- Migration of old themes; export/import of valid, invalid and extreme-value JSON.
- Scope precedence (chat > type > global).
- Safety caps for intensity and layers.

